 "script": "Tesla says its new Roadster hits sixty in under one second. It was unveiled Thursday at a SpaceX site in Texas, CBS News reported. Cold-gas thrusters built with SpaceX launched it off a ramp into a midair flip. But this car was first shown in twenty-seventeen, with deliveries promised for twenty-twenty. Here's the part that matters if you want one. Musk says production starts in twenty-twenty-eight, eleven years after the first reveal. Tesla's website says the flying version isn't approved for public roads. What would you actually use a flying car for? Tell us below.",
